Subject: publish the verified JWT payload into request.jwt.claims

PostgreSQL 18's OAuth validator interface only surfaces the authenticated
identity (authn_id -> system_user). The full, signature-verified claims sit in
a local `payload` (picojson::object) and are otherwise discarded.

This adds a single SetConfigOption call so the whole payload is published into
the session GUC `request.jwt.claims`, exactly as PostgREST sets it on
Supabase/Neon. Semantius RLS (rbac.uid()) then reads the caller's claims with
no application cooperation and no spoofing surface (Postgres set the value from
the token it just verified).

--- a/src/pg_oidc_validator.cpp
+++ b/src/pg_oidc_validator.cpp
@@ -101,6 +101,11 @@
       return false;
     }
     res->authn_id = pstrdup(payload.at(authn_field).to_str().c_str());
+    // Semantius: publish the full, signature-verified JWT payload into the
+    // session GUC request.jwt.claims so RLS can read the caller's claims,
+    // exactly as PostgREST does on Supabase/Neon.
+    SetConfigOption("request.jwt.claims",
+                    picojson::value(payload).serialize().c_str(),
+                    PGC_USERSET, PGC_S_SESSION);
   }
   PG_CATCH();
   {
